 34AL c  2013StZY: {+35}Mg was produced via the projectile fragmentation of a   
 34AL2c  345-MeV/nucleon, 70-pnA {+48}Ca{+20+} primary beam from the linear     
 34AL3c  accelerator RILAC and the four cyclotrons RRC, fRC, IRC, and SRC at    
 34AL4c  RIKEN impinging on a 15-mm-thick {+9}Be target. The secondary cocktail 
 34AL5c  beam was selected by the BigRIPS separator and the zero-degree         
 34AL6c  spectrometer (ZDS) using the B|r-|DE-ToF method, and implanted into the
 34AL7c  Cylindrical Active Implantation Target for Exotic Nuclei (CAITEN)      
 34AL8c  consisting of a segmented movable hollow-cylindrical-shaped plastic    
 34AL9c  scintillator and a stationary ring of 24 position-sensitive            
 34ALAc  photomultiplier tubes (PSPMTs) arranged on a ring inside the           
 34ALBc  scintillator at the height of the beam line. To reduce background      
 34ALCc  buildup, the scintillator barrel was rotated quickly and axially-moved 
 34ALDc  slowly in vertical direction, resulting in a helix-shaped motion. |b   
 34ALEc  particles were detected by the CAITEN and |g rays were detected using  
 34ALFc  three HPGe clover detectors. Measured E|g, I|g, |b|g-coin, and         
 34ALGc  implant-|b correlation, and deduced the T{-1/2} of {+35}Mg. Comparisons
 34ALHc  with QRPA and shell-model calculations.                                
 34AL c  1995ReZZ, 2008ReZZ: {+232}Th(p,X) E=800 MeV at Los Alamos Meson Physics
 34AL2c  Facility (LAMPF). Measured T{-1/2}, delayed neutron emission           
 34AL3c  probabilities, and average E{-n} using the Time-of-Flight Isochronous  
 34AL4c  (TOFI) spectrometer.                                                   
